    {
      "id": "twilite-product-hero",
      "type": "markdown",
      "label": "Hero",
      "root": false,
      "position": {
        "x": 1230,
        "y": -980
      },
      "width": 640,
      "height": 260,
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "data": {
        "markdown": "# Build Knowledge As A Living Graph\n\nTwilite turns graphs into durable web artifacts that humans and AI can both navigate, edit, and grow together.\n\nNot a canvas snapshot. Not a disposable chat. A structured system that stays alive as the work gets deeper.",
        "_placement": {
          "version": 1,
          "state": "auto-placed",
          "source": "layout",
          "updatedAt": 1778698422220,
          "reason": "auto-layout"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "twilite-product-difference",
      "type": "markdown",
      "label": "Why Twilite Exists",
      "root": false,
      "position": {
        "x": 1708.0004404129586,
        "y": -536.0296197830719
      },
      "width": 520,
      "height": 280,
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "data": {
        "markdown": "## Why Twilite Exists\n\nMost tools split thinking across chats, docs, tabs, whiteboards, and disconnected notes.\n\nTwilite keeps the structure itself in view.\n\nThe graph becomes the thing with value: addressable, inspectable, editable, and durable on the web.",
        "_placement": {
          "version": 1,
          "state": "manually-shaped",
          "source": "manual",
          "updatedAt": 1778699868381,
          "reason": "node-drag"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "twilite-product-how",
      "type": "markdown",
      "label": "How It Works",
      "root": false,
      "position": {
        "x": 2590,
        "y": -980
      },
      "width": 520,
      "height": 300,
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "data": {
        "markdown": "## How It Works\n\n1. Author or evolve a graph.\n2. Give it a durable address.\n3. Let humans and AI work against the same structure over time.\n\nThat lets a graph move from thought, to collaboration, to publishing, to execution without changing mediums.",
        "_placement": {
          "version": 1,
          "state": "auto-placed",
          "source": "layout",
          "updatedAt": 1778698422220,
          "reason": "auto-layout"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "twilite-product-proof",
      "type": "markdown",
      "label": "Proof",
      "root": false,
      "position": {
        "x": 755.8262921160951,
        "y": 1248.6876063734114
      },
      "width": 620,
      "height": 300,
      "ports": [
        {
          "id": "root",
          "label": "root",
          "direction": "bidirectional",
          "dataType": "any",
          "position": {
            "side": "left",
            "offset": 0.5
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "right",
          "label": "right",
          "direction": "output",
          "dataType": "any",
          "position": {
            "side": "right",
            "offset": 0.5
          }
        }
      ],
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "data": {
        "markdown": "## What Already Works Today\n\nTwilite already runs in the browser.\n\nIt already persists graphs.\nIt already exposes them at addresses.\nIt already supports AI-assisted graph authoring.\nIt already supports GitHub-backed save and publish flows.\n\nThis page is itself part of that system.",
        "_placement": {
          "version": 1,
          "state": "manually-shaped",
          "source": "manual",
          "updatedAt": 1778699490734,
          "reason": "node-drag"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "twilite-product-get-started",
      "type": "markdown",
      "label": "Get Started",
      "root": false,
      "position": {
        "x": 690,
        "y": -980
      },
      "width": 520,
      "height": 260,
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "data": {
        "markdown": "## Start Here\n\nUse this graph as a doorway into the product, not just a description of it.\n\n- Browse the product shelf.\n- Open the tutorial.\n- Explore live graph surfaces.\n- Start building something that can persist beyond one session.\n\nTwilite clicks when the graph stops being a diagram and starts being the place the work actually lives.",
        "_placement": {
          "version": 1,
          "state": "auto-placed",
          "source": "layout",
          "updatedAt": 1778698422220,
          "reason": "auto-layout"
        }
      }
    },
